     I don't think there was a warning that it shouldn't be applied to
anything but PCs (if there was, that was misleading).  It was suggested
that it wasn't _necessary_ for anything but PCs.  It turns out to be
needed for Atari TOS, and evidently RS/6000 AIX.  (Seems to me that that
suggests RS/6000 is really a PC... ;-)

> Anybody have a reasonable fix?

     Apply the "MSDOS patch" and then rebuild.

> (why can't one get color on a Unix system?)

     If you build for TERMLIB instead of TERMCAP, and if your TERMLIB
database contains color entries, then you _can_ use color on Unix by
setting both the 'color' and 'standout' options at run-time.

